    {
      "n": 7,
      "type": "why-us",
      "viewport": "all",
      "tag": "section",
      "heading": "A fixed quote, paid in stages",
      "items": [
        {
          "k": "text",
          "text": "HOW WE ESTIMATE",
          "role": "sec-label"
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "A fixed quote, paid in stages"
        },
        {
          "k": "text",
          "text": "You describe the task in a message or a short call. We ask what the site must do, which pages and languages you need and what integrations are involved, then send a written estimate with scope, timeline and price. The price is agreed before work starts."
        },
        {
          "k": "text",
          "text": "Payment is staged: we recommend 50% upfront and 50% after launch. Larger projects are split into milestones, so you only pay for work you have seen."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 8,
      "type": "why-us",
      "viewport": "all",
      "tag": "section",
      "heading": "Ukrainian agency, EU standards",
      "items": [
        {
          "k": "text",
          "text": "WHY THE PRICE IS LOWER",
          "role": "sec-label"
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Ukrainian agency, EU standards"
        },
        {
          "k": "text",
          "text": "Our prices are usually lower than Western European agency rates for one simple reason: salaries, rent and the cost of living in Ukraine are lower. That changes the price, not the tools or the result."
        },
        {
          "k": "text",
          "text": "We use the same stack as agencies in Berlin or Amsterdam — Next.js, React, TypeScript, Python, PostgreSQL, Cloudflare — and work remotely in a time zone one hour ahead of Central European Time. You get the source code and all access, staged payment and direct contact with the people building your project. See what we have built in our portfolio."
        }
      ]
    },
